    compilation warning on Clang compiler.
- solids/CSG (geom-csg-V11-04-13)
  o G4Cons: stabilise the positive quadratic root in DistanceToIn(p,v),
    avoiding spurious zero-length entries from cancellation at stave
    boundaries.
  o In G4Trap, cache a separate outward-entry rejection tolerance, offset from
    Inside's inner surface threshold by the local roundoff allowance. Prevents
    rounded departures from being accepted again as zero-distance entries;
    retain classification, inward entries and ordinary exits. Copy the new
    cache. Resolves a zero-step cycle detected in CMS geometry.
  o In G4Trd, refactored DistanceToIn(p,v) and DistanceToOut(p,v,n).
- solids/specific (geom-specific-V11-04-26)
  o G4TriangularFacet: corrected Intersect() edge tolerances to use physical
    distances, fixing false inside classifications and overlap reports for
    thin tessellated facets. Use signed edge-distance tests near boundaries
    to avoid barycentric cancellation, with a conservative barycentric filter
    for ordinary crossings and no additional per-facet storage. Fixing issue
    reported in [GitHub PR #125](https://github.com/Geant4/geant4/pull/125)
  o G4Polycone: use supporting half-planes for convex RZ classification, fixing
    false phi-face entries and zero safeties for descending-Z profiles.
    Cache slope-adjusted radial tolerances for correct normal-distance
    classification on steep inner and outer conical faces; precompute
    interpolation slopes to avoid per-query division and retain finite-edge
    checks at Z joins. Resolves few cases of zero-step cycle detected in ATLAS
    geometry.
  o G4PolyconeSide: reject spurious step-plane crossings at radial endpoints,
    preserving inward grazing exits and genuine adjoining-face crossings.
    Reject non-crossing exits at reentrant RZ joins using the adjoining face
    normal, including axial rays through step/cone corners.
    Cache corner flags and endpoint limits, and check the hit direction before
    corner tests to keep ordinary face hits fast.
    Resolves few cases of zero-step cycle detected in ATLAS geometry.
  o G4PolyhedraSide: reject non-crossing exits at reentrant RZ joins when
    the ray enters the adjoining face's half-space. Cache corner flags and
    reuse edge-normal bisectors; preserve genuine corner crossings and grazing
    contacts. Fixes cases detected in CMS geometry. 
  o G4Polyhedra: classify supporting side faces from the RZ profile to
    correctly report valid exit normals, including for convex prisms.
  o G4GenericTrap: reject outward surface re-entry in DistanceToIn(p,v), while
    preserving later intersections with concave ray profiles on twisted faces.
  o G4Ellipsoid: combine entry rejection checks to reduce branching.
    Measured approximately 15% lower exact-entry time.
  o G4Hype: simplify exit-surface tracking and defer output-normal construction.
    Measured approximately 7% lower exact-exit time without/with normals.
  o G4Tet: simplify candidate-face collection and skip normal bookkeeping for
    distance-only exit queries; measured approximately 30% lower exact-exit
    time.
  o G4EllipticalTube: reduced entry-rejection branching and reordered slab
    calculations; measured approximately 34% lower exact-entry time.
  o G4EllipticalCone: combined exit-cap branches and avoid redundant cap checks;
    measured approximately 11% lower exact-exit time without normals and 6%
    with normals.
  o G4ExtrudedSolid: cache supporting edges for valid exit normals in concave
    right prisms; retain facet-based validity for multisection extrusions.
